# Duplicate Detection & Metadata Management Walkthrough

This update introduces a robust system for managing pharmaceutical terminology with automated duplicate detection and enhanced document traceability.

## 1. Automated Duplicate Detection
When you run a **Linguistic Analysis** (extracting terms from text), the system now automatically checks if those terms already exist in your encyclopedia.

> [!TIP]
> This prevents redundant entries and ensures your scientific dictionary remains clean and professional.

- **Visual Indicator**: Terms already in the database are highlighted with an orange background and a **"ДУБЛИКАТ"** badge in the preview table.
- **Status Persistence**: These items are saved with a `duplicate_pending` status for later review.

## 2. Advanced Document Traceability (Text No)
You can now edit the **Матн №** (Text Number) for each individual term during the AI extraction phase.

- **Bulk Editing**: By default, all extracted terms inherit the current document's number.
- **Individual Overrides**: You can manually change the document reference for specific terms before saving them.

## 3. Review Workflow
In the Linguistic Encyclopedia (Annotated, Disputed, Abbreviations), we've added powerful review tools.

### Status Filtering
A new filter bar allows you to toggle between:
- **Ҳаммаси**: Show all records.
- **✅ Тасдиқланган**: Show only active, verified terms.
- **⚠️ Дубликатлар**: Focus on terms flagged for review during extraction.

### Visual Cues
Duplicate entries are marked with a thick orange border and a **"⚠️ КЎРИБ ЧИҚИЛИШИ КЕРАК"** (To be reviewed) warning to distinguish them from verified data.

## Verification Results
- **Schema Migration**: Database tables updated successfully with `status` columns.
- **AI Integration**: Claude results are successfully enriched with `is_duplicate` metadata.
- **UI Responsiveness**: Filters and edit modals updated to support the new metadata fields.
